# Shiny Stone Sales OS — Stable Development Workflow

## Process (every task)

INSPECT → PLAN → MODIFY → TEST → BUILD → VERIFY → REPORT

Never make large unrelated changes at once. Modify only files required for the task.

## Before editing

Inspect relevant files, architecture, dependencies, and affected components. Check if the feature already exists. Do not rewrite working components.

## Protected (do not change casually)

- Tailwind/PostCSS setup, `globals.css`, design tokens, typography
- Application shell, sidebar, shadcn/ui, shared UI components
- `package.json` versions (no downgrades, major upgrades, or framework swaps without explicit reason)

Prefer local component-level fixes over global CSS, root layout, or shell changes.

## After significant changes

1. Run `npm run build` — if FAIL, stop and fix before adding features
2. Use one dev server: `npm run dev` or `npm run dev:clean` (never multiple instances)
3. Verify http://localhost:3000/dashboard: CSS loads (not plain HTML), sidebar, nav, cards, no console errors
4. Regression-test shared component changes on: `/dashboard`, `/customers`, `/deals`, `/pipeline`, `/inbox`, `/purchase-orders`, `/follow-ups`, `/automation`, `/reports`, `/settings`

## Broken CSS emergency

If UI shows plain HTML, blue links, default fonts — STOP feature work. Investigate CSS imports, layout, PostCSS, compilation errors, network 404 on CSS. Clear `.next` and restart with `npm run dev:clean`. See `docs/STABILITY.md`.

## Before major architectural changes

Create a git checkpoint commit first.

## Task completion report (required)

Report: TASK | FILES CHANGED | IMPLEMENTATION | TESTING | BUILD (PASS/FAIL) | BROWSER (PASS/FAIL) | REGRESSION (PASS/FAIL) | REMAINING ISSUES

Do not report "Done" until build passes, browser styling works, feature works, and regressions are checked.

**Stability > speed.** Never leave the app broken, unstyled, or failing build.
